# 8. Coverage: JaCoCo through AGP, aggregated at the root, 75% gate

Date: ${SCAFFOLD_DATE}
Status: Accepted

## Context

The gate needs one aggregated coverage number across Android and JVM modules, including Compose code
exercised by Robolectric screen tests.

Alternatives considered:
- **Kover** — nicer DSL and annotation-based exclusions, but open AGP 9 issues (removed variant APIs,
  built-in Kotlin projects routed into the pre-9 path) at the time of this decision.

## Decision

AGP's built-in JaCoCo (`enableUnitTestCoverage` on debug) in every Android module, the `jacoco` plugin on
JVM modules, and the root convention `android-forge.root` aggregating both: `./gradlew coverageVerify`
fails below **75% line coverage**, `./gradlew coverageReport` writes HTML/XML. Robolectric-loaded classes
are counted (`includeNoLocationClasses`). Exclusions are class-file patterns: generated code and wiring
(Compose singletons, serializers, Hilt modules, entry points, `api` modules, entry builders, design tokens).

## Consequences

- Easier: works on AGP 9 with built-in Kotlin today; screens covered by screen tests count.
- Harder: exclusions are path patterns, not annotations — a new kind of generated class may need a pattern;
  revisit Kover when its AGP 9 support is complete.
